# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "An apostrophe inside a macro argument opens no parameter"

# A macro parameter opens at a parameter boundary. An apostrophe standing inside a word starts
# nothing, and a region opening there waits for a closing quote that prose never supplies — every
# construct after it then colours as that macro's arguments.

<<myMacro you'd index a relation>>
#         ^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallblock.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedure.parameters.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedure.parameter.tw-positional.tiddlywiki5 string.unquoted.html.tiddlywiki5

A paragraph standing after it.
#^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

# A quote that DOES open a parameter still opens one, whether it carries a name or stands bare.

<<myMacro 'a quoted argument'>>
#          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallblock.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedure.parameters.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedure.parameter.tw-positional.tiddlywiki5 string.quoted.single.html.tiddlywiki5

<<myMacro name='a named argument'>>
#               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedurecallblock.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedure.parameters.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.procedure.parameter.tw-name.tiddlywiki5 string.quoted.single.html.tiddlywiki5

Prose after the quoted forms.
#^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

# A DOUBLED APOSTROPHE INSIDE A WORD opens nothing either. Only the first apostrophe stood inside
# the word, so the second, standing after a quote rather than a word character, opened a region
# no closing quote ever reached, and an old-form sigil carrying bold (``''reified edge-DAG''``)
# coloured the rest of its file as arguments. An unquoted argument now carries any apostrophe
# after its first character.

<<myMacro the ''reified edge-DAG'' here>>

A paragraph after the bold.
#^^^^^^^^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5
#^^^^^^^^ - meta.variable.call.parameters.tiddlywiki5

<<myMacro x'' b>>

A paragraph after the doubled mark.
#^^^^^^^^ - meta.variable.call.parameters.tiddlywiki5

<<myMacro name=x'' b>>

A paragraph after the named form.
#^^^^^^^^ - meta.variable.call.parameters.tiddlywiki5
